# 1v1, the trace study over the whole field (BENCH-221, docs/bench/local/2026-11-09_view-rank.md, "Trace study" and
# "Per gun"; tool data/tools/learn_trace.py, PR #731). Leigh starts it once the PC is free (one card at a time, from master):
#   git checkout master && git pull
#   .\queue.ps1 run pc-learn-trace        (or  ./queue.sh run pc-learn-trace)
# One bench queue, RoboRumble workers at 0, unpinned, 12 workers, TRUTH LOG ON (the read needs it). Every step resumes;
# no step needs a decision. About 4 hours of battles (2 arms x 1,212 robots x 1 seed = 2,424 at 35 rounds), and
# about 6 GB of truth logs under work/learn-trace-pc (2.3 MB a battle on the cloud).
#
# What it is for (the PC card rule of 2026-11-03: this card changes no robot; it finds the per-opponent lines):
#   - The cloud trace study on 32 learning guns (two seeds, PR #731) found the same guns hit BeepBoop 2.0 27% less per
#     bullet than Hadur from round 0, flat by round for both, so it is not learning; the gap is largest against the
#     simpler guns; three guns barely hit BeepBoop at all (Ala 0.004 against 0.094, Defender 0.011 against 0.075,
#     QuantumChromodynamics 0.004 against 0.032). Per gun: BeepBoop stands still and shields Ala (0.4% hit, share
#     94.6; Hadur surfs it at 9.5%, share 84); it dodges Defender and QuantumChromodynamics moving. One shield line
#     for Ala read +6.85 +- 5.08 on 6 cloud seeds (pc-ala-shield confirms it).
#   - This card asks the same question of every robot in the field: against which robots does BeepBoop stand still
#     (bullets at guess factor 0, a hit rate near 0) where Hadur surfs, and against which does it take fewer hits per
#     bullet while moving; the read lists each opponent paired (bb minus c) by hit rate, damage a round and share, so
#     the candidates for shield lines and for dodger lines come out of it with their expected gains, for a per-opponent
#     card at the usual 12-seed pilot.
#   - Nothing ships from this card. One seed is enough for the per-bullet rates (thousands of bullets a battle); it is
#     not a score read.
# Stop rules (docs/bench/watch.md): halt on 30 failed battles, 60+ skipped turns a battle over the last 200 on the c arm
# (bb is another robot's jar and skips by design), or no battle in 30 minutes; every battle fought is kept and a rerun
# resumes. No dead-arm rule: bb scoring nothing against a robot is a finding, not a defect. ALERT opens an issue for
# Leigh on any stop. The bench drops broken-1.11.2.txt's robots from the set before it starts (BENCH-169).
# If the trace step cannot finish (a robot that never ends its battle), stop the queue and run the rest on the
# kept battles: .\queue.ps1 run pc-learn-trace-read (the same read and results PR, with arms.tsv rebuilt from
# the battles' rows by tools/arms_from_battles.py, since the bench writes it only when every battle has run).

set V = 3.22
set P = --parallel 12 --failed-ok
set C = --skip-build --skip-fetch --rounds 35 --cpu-constant 1488498 --child-heap 2G
set W = work/learn-trace-pc
set OUT = ../docs/bench/local
set ALERT = lgriffin

prep | git checkout -q master && mkdir -p bisect work && (cd .. && mvn -q -DskipTests package) && cp ../hadur-robot/target/hadur117.Hadur_${V}.jar bisect/ && ./fetch-opponents.sh --set census-312.txt && test -f opponents/kc.mega.BeepBoop_2.0.jar && mvn -q compile

trace | ./bench-top20.sh ${C} ${P} --set census-312.txt --seeds 1 --seed-base 11800 --arms plans/pc-learn-trace.arms --out ${W} --label learn-trace-pc --shuffle-jobs
  after: prep
  stop: fails 30
  stop: skips 60 over 200 arms c
  stop: stall 30m

read | python3 tools/arms_from_battles.py ${W} && python3 -I ../data/tools/learn_trace.py ${W} --base c --other bb --set census-312.txt --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_learn-trace-field-read.md && python3 ../data/tools/multiarm.py ${W}/arms.tsv --census census-312.txt --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_learn-trace-field.md
  after: trace

pr | bash tools/open_results_pr.sh claude/pc-learn-trace-results "1v1 trace study over the whole field: every gun against Hadur and against BeepBoop" ${OUT}/*_learn-trace-field*.md
  after: read
